  <div class="tale-introduction"><p class="eyebrow">A RIVER, A COMMUNITY AND A TRANSFORMING ENCOUNTER</p><p>This original English retelling follows <strong>Srimad Bhagavata Purana, Book 10, chapters 16–17</strong>. It traces the episode from the poisoned lake through Kaliya’s departure and Krishna’s return to the people of Vraja. The prayers and conflict are condensed without reproducing a modern translation.</p></div>
  <section class="story-characters" aria-labelledby="characters-title"><p class="eyebrow">MEET THE CHARACTERS</p><h2 id="characters-title">Characters in this story</h2><dl>
    <div><dt>Krishna</dt><dd>The young cowherd who enters the poisoned water and restores the Yamuna.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Kaliya</dt><dd>A powerful serpent whose presence has made the lake deadly.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>The Nagapatnis</dt><dd>Kaliya’s wives, who approach Krishna with their children and pray for mercy.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Balarama</dt><dd>Krishna’s elder brother, calm amid the fear on the riverbank.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Yashoda and Nanda</dt><dd>Krishna’s parents in Vraja, drawn to the Yamuna with the frightened community.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>The people and cattle of Vraja</dt><dd>The community whose lives depend upon Krishna and the river.</dd></div>
  </dl></section>
